{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-logistics-route-013-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/RouteEscrowFireTests.cs", "line": 463, "method": "CrashedDisposition_StillDebitsSource", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Logistics/RouteOrchestrator.cs EmitPickupHalf; remove the pickup debit -> red, but that is the same line Shuttle_DebitsRefineryAtItsWindow_EscrowEmptyAfterCycle already pins; no disposition-dependent line exists to mutate.", "what_it_asserts": "That a shuttle route's refinery window debits its source and releases the reservation on a single eligible tick.", "why_weak": "The named variable (a crashed transport disposition) is never set or varied: the route fixture has no disposition field and the test's own comment says the firing path does not consult one. The register records 19.2.5 coverage that no assertion carries, and the body duplicates the first tick of the Shuttle test at line 363.", "proposed_action": "Either delete it and note 19.2.5 as covered by reading, or give it real content: set the recording/route terminal disposition that a future gate could read and assert the debit still fires, so a gate added later reds here.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-logistics-route-013-02", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/RouteEscrowFireTests.cs", "line": 396, "method": "PartialCycle_UnfiredWindowReservationLive_CompetingRouteSeesIt", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Logistics/LiveRouteRuntimeEnvironment.cs:334; drop the OtherRoutesReservedFor subtraction from the net-available wrap -> this test stays green (the subtraction it checks is written in the test body).", "what_it_asserts": "That after window 0 fires, source B's 200 Ore reservation is still live and OtherRoutesReservedFor returns 200 for a competing route id.", "why_weak": "The headline claim ('competing route sees it') is asserted by test-side arithmetic (250.0 - otherReserved == 50.0), a tautology; the production net wrap and the RoutePickupSourceGate hold it feeds are never called, so a regression that keeps the escrow row but stops netting it leaves this green.", "proposed_action": "Replace the inline subtraction with a call through the real gate (RoutePickupSourceGate with a live-amount reader returning 250 for pid 200) and assert the competing route holds with the source-reserved token naming this route.", "effort": "M", "july_ref": "none"}
